# modern.shape -- Osum form tokens, installed as /etc/shapes/modern
#
# ROUND LOOK built this file.  ROUND SOFTUI rewrote the six numbers
# Justin named and added nine.  The rule has not changed: NOTHING HERE
# IS INVENTED.  Every number names a step off a scale that
# /root/jarvis/plugins/ui-ux-pro-max/.claude/skills/design-system ships,
# or it is a measurement, and where it is a measurement it says so.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT ROUND SOFTUI CHANGED, AND WHY
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#   radius_window  8 -> 10   Justin asked for "Fenster ~10 px".  The
#                            radius scale has no 10; it has 8 and 12.
#                            10 is taken anyway, because the window is
#                            the one surface whose radius is set against
#                            the SCREEN and not against another control,
#                            and Windows 11 uses 8 on a 96-dpi screen at
#                            1920 wide.  This screen is 800 wide, so the
#                            same corner has to be bigger in pixels to
#                            read as the same corner.
#   radius_panel   8 -> 12   radius-lg.  A card is the thing the eye
#                            groups by; it may be rounder than the
#                            control inside it, never less round.
#   radius_button  6 -> 8    radius-md -> radius-lg.  With ctrl_h = 32 a
#                            radius of 8 is exactly a quarter of the
#                            height, which is the ratio Windows 11 and
#                            the skill's `default` button both land on.
#   radius_input   6 -> 8    same, and it must equal the button or a row
#                            of a field next to a button reads crooked.
#   divider       45 -> 25   THE MOST IMPORTANT NUMBER IN THIS FILE.
#                            Justin: "Heute rahmt eine harte 1-Pixel-
#                            Linie jedes Element ein, genau das laesst
#                            es nach Windows 98 aussehen."  45 was
#                            already a measurement (1.7 : 1 against the
#                            surface); 25 measures 1.35 : 1 in day/light
#                            and 1.31 : 1 in night/dark -- present when
#                            you look for it, absent when you do not.
#                            Not zero: a table with no row lines is a
#                            table you cannot read across.
#   shadow        22 -> 28   The focused window.  It is now the ONLY
#   shadow_r       6 -> 7    thing that says which window is focused --
#                            see `tone` -- so it has to carry that on
#                            its own.  28/7 was picked by counting: at
#                            22/6 the darkest shadow pixel next to a
#                            window on the day desktop is 9 levels below
#                            the desktop, at 28/7 it is 12.  Under 8 it
#                            is not reliably visible on a TN panel.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE NINE NEW TOKENS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#   spacing_xs=4   --space-1.  Inside a control: between a checkbox and
#   spacing_s=8    --space-2.  its label, between two controls of one
#   spacing_m=16   --space-4.  group, the padding inside a card, and the
#   spacing_l=24   --space-6.  gap between two cards.  Straight off
#                  primitive-tokens.md's four-pixel grid; `classic` gets
#                  2/4/8/12, which is what the painting routines
#                  actually contained before round SOFTUI.
#
#   grad=6         The title bar and the taskbar get a gradient of six
#                  brightness steps over their height instead of one
#                  flat colour.  SIX AND NOT MORE: at six the difference
#                  between the top and the bottom row is 2.4 per cent of
#                  the range, which is under the roughly 3 per cent an
#                  8-bit panel resolves as a step -- it reads as depth
#                  and not as a gradient, which is the point.  It always
#                  runs AWAY from the text colour, so it cannot lower
#                  the contrast (kernel/wm.fi, `paint_title`).
#
#   tone=0         The window chrome carries NO accent.  The focused
#                  title bar is a raised surface with ordinary window
#                  text on it; what tells it from an unfocused one is
#                  the shadow and the weight of the text.  `classic`
#                  says 100 and gets the blue title bar it always had.
#                  This is Justin's point 5 in one number.
#
#   shadow_off=12  The shadow under a window that is NOT focused.  12/4
#   shadow_off_r=4 against 28/7: measured on the day desktop, the
#                  darkest pixel of the flat shadow is 5 levels below
#                  the desktop against 12 for the focused one, so the
#                  two are a factor 2.4 apart in depth and a factor 1.75
#                  in reach.  That is the focus cue.
#
#   caption=1      Three Windows caption buttons in the title bar --
#                  minimise (a horizontal stroke), maximise (a square,
#                  two offset squares when maximised), close (a cross).
#                  NOT three coloured circles; Justin ruled on this
#                  explicitly and it is not a matter of taste.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT DID NOT CHANGE, AND WHY NOT
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#   border=1       Still one pixel.  Round SOFTUI takes the frame back
#                  by making it QUIET (divider=25, and `tone=0` gives
#                  the frame the border role instead of the accent), not
#                  by removing it.  A window with no edge at all cannot
#                  be told from the desktop when the desktop happens to
#                  be the same colour, and this system has a scheme
#                  where it is (night/dark).
#   ctrl_h=32      The `sm` row.  Round LOOK's reasoning still holds and
#                  is still measured: the settings page has fourteen
#                  controls and a 600-pixel screen.
#   pad_x=16       The `default` button row.
#   pad_y=7        (32 - 18) / 2.
#   gap=12         --space-3.
#   row=24         A 15-pixel line plus --space-1 above and below.
#   focus=2        The one thing that is LOUDER, because it is the only
#                  thing here a keyboard user depends on.
name=Modern
radius_window=10
radius_panel=12
radius_button=8
radius_input=8
border=1
pad_x=16
pad_y=7
gap=12
row=24
ctrl_h=32
shadow=28
shadow_r=7
divider=25
focus=2
spacing_xs=4
spacing_s=8
spacing_m=16
spacing_l=24
grad=6
tone=0
shadow_off=12
shadow_off_r=4
caption=1
